# netsurf: a change that changes the root's own style restyles the root in place (patch 459)
# Generated 2026-11-27
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 458)
#
# html_rl_doc_noop's walk declined whenever the root <html>'s own style
# changed ("an element's style changes, HTML": bbc's sheet removals, most
# of what is left of "detached stylesheet pruned"; root changes too), as
# everything inherits from it. But the walk cascades the root's children
# against its NEW style (root_new), so every element under it is still
# compared, and those that change are hits (447). Only the root's box needs
# the new style: taken in place -- out of keep[] and owned here, swapped in
# after the context install and before the hits' restyles (they read
# c->layout->style as the root's), unit_len_ctx.root_style repointed, as
# html_reconvert_fast_style swaps a box's styles -- when construction would
# decide the same (display, float, position), no ::before / ::after
# changes (the diff says so) and nothing counts; then the page is laid out
# whole (html_rl_root_relayout_now). Inherited changes still mostly reach
# more than 8 elements and keep the full rebuild.
#
